    "#include <stdio.h>",
    "",
    "void* thread_function(void* arg) {",
    "    printf(\"New thread running\\n\");",
    "    return NULL;",
    "}",
    "",
    "int main() {",
    "    pthread_t thread_id;",
    "    pthread_create(&thread_id, NULL, thread_function, NULL);",
    "    pthread_join(thread_id, NULL);  // Wait for the thread to finish",
    "    return 0;",
    "}"
  ],
  "example_explanation": "This example demonstrates pthread_create by creating a new thread that runs the thread_function, which simply prints a message. The main function calls pthread_create with default attributes, passing NULL as the argument. The pthread_join ensures the main thread waits for the new thread to complete, showing how the new thread executes concurrently while sharing the process's resources."
}
